## Image Management

### Disk Image Concepts

```
Disk Image Hierarchy:
┌───────────────────┐
│   Full Image      │
│  (Complete copy)  │
└────────┬──────────┘
         │
    ┌────┴────────────┐
    │                 │
┌───▼────┐        ┌───▼────┐
│Snapshot│        │Snapshot│
│(Point  │        │(Point  │
│in time)│        │in time)│
└────────┘        └────────┘
```

### Image Operations

```
Create Image:
ICEMAN IMAGE-CREATE
  FROM-VOL(source-volume)
  TO-DEVICE(tape-device)
  COMPRESSION(ZLIB)
  ENCRYPTION(AES-256)

Restore Image:
ICEMAN IMAGE-RESTORE
  FROM-DEVICE(tape-device)
  TO-VOL(target-volume)
  VERIFY(YES)

Verify Image:
ICEMAN IMAGE-VERIFY
  IMAGE-ID(image-number)
  CHECKSUM-VALIDATION
  REPORT-ERRORS
```

### Image Types

```
Full Image:
├─ Complete disk copy
├─ Large size (entire volume)
└─ Used for disaster recovery

Incremental Image:
├─ Only changed blocks
├─ Smaller size
└─ Faster creation

Snapshot:
├─ Point-in-time copy
├─ Minimal space overhead
└─ Quick recovery capability
```

